#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Cyberpunk audio console -- waybar pulseaudio on-click. Centered 1080p window.

Three pages (all live-synced against pactl / amixer on a poll timer):
  PLAYBACK  -- matrix: every playing app (rows) x every output (columns); click a cell to
               move the app there. BUSES rows (virtual sinks) send to outputs via
               module-loopback. Output headers carry volume / mute / default.
  RECORDING -- same matrix for mic-capture apps x input devices.
  INTERFACE -- the Focusrite's own mixer (ALSA controls), generic: enum -> pills,
               switch -> toggle, integer -> slider; plus a STANDARD ROUTING reset.
Rows stay alive across polls and update in place (a live GtkScale must not be rebuilt
under a drag); `self._dragging` guards sliders mid-drag. If the set of columns changes
the matrix is rebuilt from scratch (rare: a device appears/disappears).
"""

